<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">III-B</span> </span><span id="S3.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Preliminary AI Agent Settings</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">VibeCodeHPC supports flexible multi-agent configuration. For this experiment, we implemented the agents from Fig. <a href="#S2.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ II-A System Overview ‣ II VibeCodeHPC ‣ VibeCodeHPC: An Agent-Based Iterative Prompting Auto-Tuner for HPC Code Generation Using LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> with specific role assignments using Claude Code functionalities. Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="TABLE I ‣ III-B Preliminary AI Agent Settings ‣ III Performance Evaluation ‣ VibeCodeHPC: An Agent-Based Iterative Prompting Auto-Tuner for HPC Code Generation Using LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a> lists the implemented AI agents.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The system employs a project-manager-style AI agent architecture where each agent handles a subset of functions from Fig. <a href="#S2.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ II-A System Overview ‣ II VibeCodeHPC ‣ VibeCodeHPC: An Agent-Based Iterative Prompting Auto-Tuner for HPC Code Generation Using LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Note that the Continuous Delivery (CD) agent, which manages generated code, does not directly perform any roles defined in Fig. <a href="#S2.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ II-A System Overview ‣ II VibeCodeHPC ‣ VibeCodeHPC: An Agent-Based Iterative Prompting Auto-Tuner for HPC Code Generation Using LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE I: </span>Implemented AI agents in this experiment</figcaption>
