<td id="S3.T2.1.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Bigger tiling sizes / Failed</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.1.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.1.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b">v1.5.1</td>
<td id="S3.T2.1.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_b">TBD</td>
<td id="S3.T2.1.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_b">TBD</td>
<td id="S3.T2.1.8.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b">Boundary condition / Pending</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For a summary of the multi-agent activity in Fig. <a href="#S3.F3" title="Fig. 3 ‣ III-D Preliminary Result ‣ III Performance Evaluation ‣ VibeCodeHPC: An Agent-Based Iterative Prompting Auto-Tuner for HPC Code Generation Using LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, the following role-based contributions were made:</p>
<ul id="S3.I7" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I7.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PM</span>: Overall project management, resource allocation, termination decisions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I7.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SE1</span>: Continuous monitoring, statistical analysis, SOTA management, report creation.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I7.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PG1.1</span>: Implemented v1.0.0, v1.0.1, v1.3.0 (invalid), v1.5.1 (Pending).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I7.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I7.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I7.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PG1.2</span>: Implemented v1.4.0 (the best performance).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I7.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I7.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I7.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PG1.3</span>: Implemented v1.5.0 (failed).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I7.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I7.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I7.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CD</span>: GitHub management, requirements violation detection.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Through this experiment, the following advantages of the multi-agent version over the solo-agent version can be identified.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S3.I8" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Rapid trial of multiple optimizations through multi-agent parallel development</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Quick detection and handling of requirements violations (v1.3.0)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I8.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I8.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I8.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Real-time monitoring and statistical updates</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Fig. <a href="#S3.F4" title="Fig. 4 ‣ III-D Preliminary Result ‣ III Performance Evaluation ‣ VibeCodeHPC: An Agent-Based Iterative Prompting Auto-Tuner for HPC Code Generation Using LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> illustrates Claude Code’s token consumption from the start of execution for both solo-agent and multi-agent cases, reflecting each agent’s activity. The graph is automatically generated by the Context Usage Report shown in Fig. <a href="#S2.F2" title="Fig. 2 ‣ II-D Dynamic Inter-Agent Monitoring ‣ II VibeCodeHPC ‣ VibeCodeHPC: An Agent-Based Iterative Prompting Auto-Tuner for HPC Code Generation Using LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">In Claude Code, when the configured token limit is exceeded, an auto-compact process occurs, reducing the available memory (context window). Consequently, the agents’ memory may periodically disappear. As shown in Fig. <a href="#S3.F4" title="Fig. 4 ‣ III-D Preliminary Result ‣ III Performance Evaluation ‣ VibeCodeHPC: An Agent-Based Iterative Prompting Auto-Tuner for HPC Code Generation Using LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, auto-compact is triggered when the agents exceed approximately 150K tokens.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">In the multi-agent version in Fig. <a href="#S3.F4" title="Fig. 4 ‣ III-D Preliminary Result ‣ III Performance Evaluation ‣ VibeCodeHPC: An Agent-Based Iterative Prompting Auto-Tuner for HPC Code Generation Using LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> (b), the PM starts first, followed by SE and PG1.1 generating code. The additional programmer agent PG1.3 participates in the second phase, after the initial token limit. In the third phase, all agents are involved, but their activity is lower compared to the earlier phases.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="S3.F4.1" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:165.6pt;"><img src="2510.00031v1/fig/fig4a.png" id="S3.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:229/152;" width="229" height="152" alt="Refer to caption">
<p id="S3.F4.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">(a) Solo-agent</p>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="S3.F4.2" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:165.6pt;"><img src="2510.00031v1/fig/fig4b.png" id="S3.F4.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:229/152;" width="229" height="152" alt="Refer to caption">
<p id="S3.F4.2.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">(b) Multi-agents</p>
</div></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 4: </span>Claude’s context length (tokens) time transition.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS5.4" class="ltx_text">III-E</span> </span><span id="S3.SS5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Discussion</span></h3>

<section id="S3.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S3.SS5.SSS1.4" class="ltx_text">III-E</span>1 </span>Achieved Performance and Multi-agent Behavior</h4>

<div id="S3.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the solo-agent case shown in Fig. <a href="#S3.F3" title="Fig. 3 ‣ III-D Preliminary Result ‣ III Performance Evaluation ‣ VibeCodeHPC: An Agent-Based Iterative Prompting Auto-Tuner for HPC Code Generation Using LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, only 24.1% of the theoretical peak performance was achieved. As a result, the project was gracefully terminated after 35 minutes, although the target execution time was set to 2–3 hours. In addition, the solo-agent failed to push the code to GitHub and improperly employed cuBLAS-based coding, which was explicitly prohibited in the requirements. We believe this behavior resulted from memory loss when the agent process was suspended (auto-compacted in Claude Code).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In contrast, the multi-agent version can mutually monitor whether the specifications are being satisfied. Therefore, it not only reduces violations of the requirement definitions but also enables the use of active memory for improved code generation. In other words, these can be considered decisive advantages of the multi-agent approach over the solo-agent approach.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Interestingly, although the PG achieved high performance, the CD issued a warning regarding the implementation that violated the requirements by using cuBLAS, and the PM ordered an emergency stop. This is a noteworthy interaction in the multi-agent system. Listing <a href="#LST2" title="Listing 2 ‣ III-E1 Achieved Performance and Multi-agent Behavior ‣ III-E Discussion ‣ III Performance Evaluation ‣ VibeCodeHPC: An Agent-Based Iterative Prompting Auto-Tuner for HPC Code Generation Using LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows these interactions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="LST2" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float">Listing 2: </span>Interaction in the multi-agent system.</figcaption>
<div id="LST2.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_language_XML ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx15" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">PG1</span><span id="lstnumberx15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">.1</span><span id="lstnumberx15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">:</span><span id="lstnumberx15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_string ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">"[SE1]<span id="lstnumberx15.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>I<span id="lstnumberx15.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>have<span id="lstnumberx15.5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>reviewed<span id="lstnumberx15.5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>the<span id="lstnumberx15.5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>codes<span id="lstnumberx15.5.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>of<span id="lstnumberx15.5.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>v1.3.0<span id="lstnumberx15.5.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>and<span id="lstnumberx15.5.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>v1.4.0.<span id="lstnumberx15.5.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>Please<span id="lstnumberx15.5.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>report<span id="lstnumberx15.5.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>the<span id="lstnumberx15.5.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>job<span id="lstnumberx15.5.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>execution<span id="lstnumberx15.5.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>status."</span>
</div>
